The body of a limit=0 standards request. VERBATIM, character for character, from the gate G-1 result
in 01-sdk-v3.md section 12:

  Result, run 2026-08-02 against devel partner sws: PASS. GET
  https://api.abconnect.instructure.com/rest/v4.1/standards?limit=0&... returned HTTP 200 with
  {"meta":{"count":1471199,"offset":0,"took":181,"limit":0}}

Why this fixture matters more than its size suggests: there is no "data" member and no "links" member.
ABPage<T> declares Data, Meta, and Links as required, so deserializing this body straight into
ABPage<Standard> raises a JsonException for missing required members even though AB Connect answered
correctly. This is the body that PageRequest.MetaOnly produces, and it is why the internal
ABPageDocument<TResource> wire shape exists: it deserializes with every member optional and projects
absent data to an empty list and absent links to an all-null PageLinks, preserving Invariant E1
without turning a correct 200 into a format error.
